menu "Performance Pots"

config AMYSYNTH_POT_CUTOFF_GPIO
    int "Filter-cutoff pot GPIO (ADC1 channel, -1 = disabled)"
    default -1
    range -1 10
    help
        Analog performance controls read from the ESP32-S3 ADC1 unit
        (GPIO1..10; one channel per pot). A low-priority task samples each
        enabled pin at ~20 Hz, smooths it, and pushes the value into the
        synth only when it moves past a small deadband.
        -1 (the default) disables the role, so the upstream devkit is
        unaffected; boards with spare ADC1 pads set the pins here.
        Each symbol defaults to -1; all three can coexist.

config AMYSYNTH_POT_FX_GPIO
    int "FX pot GPIO (ADC1 channel, -1 = disabled)"
    default -1
    range -1 10
    help
        Acts as a MIDI CC1 mod wheel into the wireless live-play slot when
        the wireless synth is compiled in: the 20 Hz live_play LFO stepper
        turns the position into a ~4 Hz osc-0 vibrato (depth ramps up to +-1
        semitone at full travel, 0 = no vibrato). Without the wireless synth
        (upstream devkit) it maps onto the global echo + reverb sends
        (0..100%) instead.

config AMYSYNTH_POT_VOLUME_GPIO
    int "Master-volume pot GPIO (ADC1 channel, -1 = disabled)"
    default -1
    range -1 10
    help
        Maps the pot onto AMY's global master volume (0..2x, unity in the
        middle). Directly scales the rendered mix before it reaches any
        output.

endmenu